/api.github.com/users/tgolen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/73647","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This is part of deprecating Onyx.connect. [Parent Issue](https://github.com/Expensify/Expensify/issues/522215)\n\n## Details\n- **Module**: [src/libs/actions/Report.ts](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/main/src/libs/actions/Report.ts)\n- **Onyx Key**: `ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.REPORT_ACTIONS`\n- **Reference**: `Line 313: ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.REPORT_ACTIONS`\n\nBe sure to refactor methods using test driven development:\n1. Create a unit test for methods before refactoring\n2. Refactor the methods\n3. Ensure the unit test still runs after refactoring\n4. Reinforce the unit testing with a functional test and a QA test\n5. Once you are done, decrease the number of allowable ESLint warnings [here](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/e7b5ac9401e2ae9b5c2c70ec513e8de6f5279d7d/package.json#L48) to equal the number of `Onyx.connect` references remaining in the code\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Issue Owner</summary>Current Issue Owner: @eVoloshchak</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/73651/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/73651/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/2","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/2/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/2/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/2/events","html_url":"https://github.com/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/2","id":4577270407,"node_id":"I_kwDOSvpFLM8AAAABENOahw","number":2,"title":"Fix typo in README","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11128329926,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSvpFLM8AAAACl0zWxg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057ff","default":true,"description":"Good for new contributors."},{"id":11128350030,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSvpFLM8AAAACl00lTg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"e4e669","default":false,"description":"Reward-backed contribution task."},{"id":11128350083,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSvpFLM8AAAACl00lgw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/labels/AI%20agent%20friendly","name":"AI agent friendly","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Suitable for autonomous AI agents."},{"id":11128350237,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSvpFLM8AAAACl00mHQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/labels/%F0%9F%92%8E%20Bounty","name":"💎 Bounty","color":"0075ca","default":false,"description":"Highlighted bounty issue."},{"id":11128808571,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSvpFLM8AAAACl1Qkew","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/labels/$50","name":"$50","color":"34d399","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":82,"created_at":"2026-06-03T05:50:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:29:19Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Review the README for minor spelling, grammar, or formatting issues and submit a small cleanup PR.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Keep the pull request focused.\n- Include a short summary of the change.\n- Link this issue in the pull request description.\n\n/bounty $50","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/2/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xevrion-v2/agent-playground/issues/2/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/aspire/issues/18232","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/aspire","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/aspire/issues/18232/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/aspire/issues/18232/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/aspire/issues/18232/events","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/issues/18232","id":4671651673,"node_id":"I_kwDOKYQzfc8AAAABFnO_WQ","number":18232,"title":"📈 CI Daily Pulse","user":{"login":"radical","id":1472,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/radical","html_url":"https://github.com/radical","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radical/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radical/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radical/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radical/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radical/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radical/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radical/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radical/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radical/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":6076621027,"node_id":"LA_kwDOKYQzfc8AAAABajHg4w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/aspire/labels/area-engineering-systems","name":"area-engineering-systems","color":"d4c5f9","default":false,"description":"infrastructure helix infra engineering repo stuff"},{"id":9982027626,"node_id":"LA_kwDOKYQzfc8AAAACUvmnag","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/aspire/labels/automated","name":"automated","color":"281af4","default":false,"description":"Opened by bots or tools"},{"id":10927001707,"node_id":"LA_kwDOKYQzfc8AAAACi0zQaw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/aspire/labels/triage:bot-seen","name":"triage:bot-seen","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":"Aspire triage bot has seen this issue"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":239,"created_at":"2026-06-16T06:26:45Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:26:11Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# 🔴 outerloop — new mobile-nav test regression · 🟡 GH main red at tip (flaky CLI) · 🟢 internal 80% · 🟢 PR 76% (green tip) — **1 item for a dev**\n\n> ### 🔴 For a dev — outerloop's new mobile-nav Playwright test fails on every OS\n> **What:** [`MobileNavMenuClosesWhenFocusLeavesMenu`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28838538090) — the new Playwright E2E test added by [#18502](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/pull/18502) asserts the mobile nav menu closes when focus leaves it, but gets `Expected: True, Actual: False` on **both ubuntu-latest and windows-latest**. **Deterministic** — it failed all 4 attempts (outerloop auto-rerun is spent), so it will not self-heal.\n> **Do:** a dev (the #18502 author) should fix the test or the behavior — [failed outerloop run](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28838538090) · `tests/Aspire.Dashboard.Tests/Integration/Playwright/MobileNavMenuTests.cs:42`.\n>\n> <sub>Secondary live signal: **GH main is red at the tip** on a recurring flaky CLI tree-kill [timeout](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28843804933) (intermittent, 2× in 36h, no auto-rerun on rolling) — worth a dev's eye but it self-heals on the next push. Everything else red = PR flakes the rerun bot is absorbing, or yesterday's infra blips gone quiet — see § 🧩 below.</sub>\n\n<sub>Window: **Sun Jul 5 18:12 → Tue Jul 7 06:12 UTC** (last 36h) · Δ vs 7-day average · Jul 7, 2026.</sub>\n\n### 📊 Last 36h by lane — activity, pass rate & Δ vs 7d\n\n| Lane | 36h activity | 36h pass rate (Δ vs 7d) | Latest build |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [**🌳 GH CI — main**](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/workflows/ci.yml?query=event%3Apush+branch%3Amain) | 🟩🟩🟩🟩🟩🟥🟥 | 🔴 69% (9/13) · ▲ 15.4 | 🔴 [Jul 7 05:27](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28843804933) |\n| [**🧪 GH CI outerloop — main**](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/workflows/tests-outerloop.yml?query=event%3Aschedule+branch%3Amain) | 🟩🟩🟥 | 🔴 50% (1/2, 95% CI 9–91%) · ▼ 35.7 | 🔴 [Jul 7 03:05](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28838538090) |\n| [**🏗️ Internal (AzDO) — main**](https://dev.azure.com/dnceng/internal/_build?definitionId=1602) | 🟩🟩🟩🟩🟩🟥 | 🟢 80% (8/10) · ▼ 2.4 | 🟢 [Jul 7 01:17](https://dev.azure.com/dnceng/internal/_build/results?buildId=3015923&view=results) |\n| [**🔀 GH CI — PR validation**](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/workflows/ci.yml?query=event%3Apull_request) ⭐ | 🟩🟩🟩🟩🟩🟩🟩🟥🟥 | 🟢 76% (26/34) · ▼ 12.4 | 🟢 [Jul 7 06:07](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28845393228) |\n\n🧱 **infra share: 86% (6/7)** — six of seven rolling failures this window were environmental / flaky (4 GH-main infra+flake blips + 2 internal aggregate); the lone product/test regression is outerloop's new #18502 Playwright test · latest failed internal build [Jul 6 05:25](https://dev.azure.com/dnceng/internal/_build/results?buildId=3015220&view=results).\n\n<sub>bar length = sample size / confidence (short = read its % with care) · `Δ vs 7d` = 36h rate minus the lane's 7-day average · Latest build = red/green of the lane's most recent in-window run, linked to it · lane names link to the workflow / pipeline. Release lanes omitted (no builds in window).</sub>\n\n### 🧩 What's broken & why\n\n**One thing needs a human: outerloop main is broken by a real test regression — [#18502](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/pull/18502)'s new mobile-nav Playwright test fails on every OS and no bot will fix it (outerloop reruns are already spent).** GH main is red at the tip on a recurring flaky CLI timeout worth a dev's eye but it self-heals; everything else is flaky noise the rerun bot is absorbing on PRs, or yesterday's infra blips gone quiet.\n\n|  | What's broken | Who's on it | Since |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 🔴 | **Outerloop main** — the new mobile-nav-menu Playwright test from [#18502](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/pull/18502) fails on **both** ubuntu & windows: the menu doesn't close when focus leaves it (`Expected True, Actual False`). Merged Jul 6 23:26; the first [outerloop run](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28838538090) after it went red. | **Needs a dev — won't self-heal** (outerloop auto-rerun spent at attempt 4); the #18502 author owns the fix | red since the first run after merge, ~3h ago |\n| 🟡 | **GH main** — red at the tip on a flaky CLI tree-kill [timeout](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28843804933) (a process-tree-kill test timed out while the runner sat at 96.5% CPU). Recurred twice in the window; **intermittent** — the run just before it passed. | **Needs a dev to triage — no auto-rerun on rolling**; a recurring flake worth quarantining, though it self-heals on the next push | red at the tip, last failed ~45m ago |\n| 🟡 | **PR validation** — 8 of 34 PR runs red on **their own** checks, all attempt 4+ (bot's 3 retries spent): CLI E2E smoke, a Dashboard a11y branch, a TypeScript-polyglot branch, a VS Code-extension dep-bump, a darc dependency-flow branch, a localization branch. | **Rerun bot is absorbing these** (PR-only) — no repo-level cause; lane green at the tip | freshest red ~1h ago, [tip green](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28845393228) |\n| ⚪ | **Internal (AzDO) main** — 2 builds failed; aggregate results only, no confirmable code regression. | **Looks already fixed** — [latest build green](https://dev.azure.com/dnceng/internal/_build/results?buildId=3015923&view=results) | last failed ~25h ago, green at tip |\n\n🧱 **Product vs infra:** today's only product/test regression is outerloop's new [#18502](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/pull/18502) Playwright test. GH main's failures are all environmental / flaky (an SDK-download 404, a runner that lost communication, and a recurring CLI timeout under runner CPU load), and internal's 2 are aggregate builds that already recovered.\n\n⏱️ PR validation's build-time p50 reads high (**~25m vs ~13m** 7d-avg), but that's **rerun wall-clock inflation on a thin holiday sample** (34 runs) — the red PR runs are attempt-4+ reruns whose end-to-end time spans every attempt, not a product slowdown.\n\n<details><summary>exact tests, jobs &amp; counts</summary>\n\n**🔴 Outerloop — main — 1 in-window failure ([`28838538090`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28838538090), Jul 7 03:05, att 4 — outerloop reruns exhausted):**\n- Failed `outerloop_tests / Dashboard / Dashboard (ubuntu-latest)` **and** `(windows-latest)` — same test both OSes: `Aspire.Dashboard.Tests.Integration.Playwright.MobileNavMenuTests.MobileNavMenuClosesWhenFocusLeavesMenu` — `Assert.True() Failure: Expected True, Actual False` at `tests/Aspire.Dashboard.Tests/Integration/Playwright/MobileNavMenuTests.cs:42`.\n- This 238-line Playwright test file was **added by [#18502](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/pull/18502)** (adamint, \"Keep mobile nav focus visible at high zoom\", merged Jul 6 23:26). The prior outerloop run [`28765089106`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28765089106) (Jul 6 03:06) — before #18502 — passed; the first scheduled run after the merge went red. Deterministic across both OSes and all 4 attempts ⇒ a real regression, not a flake.\n\n**🟡 GH CI — main — 4 in-window failures (9/13 passed); the tip is the only one still live, the other 3 self-healed:**\n- [`28843804933`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28843804933) (Jul 7 05:27, **tip**) — `Cli (windows-latest)`: `Aspire.Cli.Tests.Projects.ProcessGuestLauncherTests.LaunchAsync_WithGracefulServices_ProcessIgnoresSignal_ExpireEscalatesToTreeKill` — `System.TimeoutException : The operation has timed out` at `tests/Aspire.Cli.Tests/Projects/ProcessGuestLauncherTests.cs:224`; heartbeat shows runner CPU at 96.5% (csc-bound). No green run after it yet.\n- [`28769573150`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28769573150) (Jul 6 05:18) — same `Cli (windows-latest)` tree-kill timeout flake (2nd occurrence in window).\n- [`28769496423`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28769496423) (Jul 6 05:16) — dotnet-SDK download 404 (CDN infra). Both 05:1x failures self-healed at [06:00](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28771147749).\n- [`28824142784`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28824142784) (Jul 6 21:21) — `windows-latest` runner lost communication (runner infra, not a test). Self-healed at [23:26](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28830258778).\n\n**🟡 PR validation — 8 in-window failure runs across 7 branches, all attempt 4+ (bot exhausted its 3 retries):**\n- [`28831166411`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28831166411) — `darc-main-b30d48fe…` (automated dependency flow) — many `Hosting.*` container-integration jobs (ubuntu).\n- [`28802176775`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28802176775) · [`28789776853`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28789776853) · [`28785557421`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28785557421) — `feature/filechooser-interaction-input` — `Cli.EndToEnd-SmokeTests` / `-DotnetToolSmokeTests` (ubuntu), its own feature area.\n- [`28814672091`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28814672091) — `feat/deno-typescript-apphost-toolchain` — `Cli.EndToEnd-TypeScriptPolyglotTests` (ubuntu), its own feature area.\n- [`28787305306`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28787305306) — `dapine/security/open-alerts-2026-06-27` (security dep-bump) — `Run VS Code extension unit tests (Windows)`.\n- [`28822552561`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28822552561) — `adamint/a11y-17657-mobile-focus` — `Dashboard` / `Dashboard.Components` (its own accessibility area; same author + area as #18502).\n- [`28842215857`](https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/actions/runs/28842215857) (att 2) — `copilot/localize-validation-messages` — `Hosting-1 (windows-latest)` integration test.\n\n**⚪ Internal (AzDO) main — 2 in-window failed builds (8/10 passed), aggregate results only (privacy — counts, no job names):**\n- build `3015086` (Jul 5 23:43) · build [`3015220`](https://dev.azure.com/dnceng/internal/_build/results?buildId=3015220&view=results) (Jul 6 05:25, latest failed). Recovered — tip [3015923](https://dev.azure.com/dnceng/internal/_build/results?buildId=3015923&view=results) (Jul 7 01:17) green.\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>🔴 needs a human now · 🟡 keep an eye on it · ⚪ looks resolved — these are **distinct** from the lane table's 🔴/🟢 run-outcome dots.</sub>\n\n### 🔁 Reruns & flaky tax\n\nThe **auto-rerun bot carries the flaky tax** — 8 of 11 red→green rescues were the bot's (PR-only); humans hand-reran 8 times for 3 more rescues, so some manual toil on top but the bot did the bulk.\n\n<details><summary>rerun actor split (last 36h)</summary>\n\n- 🤖 **Auto-rerun bot:** 31 reruns across 17 PR runs → **8 rescued** red→green; 6 still red, 3 cancelled.\n- 🧑 **Manual (human) reruns:** 8 reruns across 5 PR runs (1 branches the bot also reran) → on the 4 human-only branches: **3 rescued**, 1 still red, 0 cancelled.\n- 🔗 **Combined: 22 distinct PR runs** needed a rerun in the window (11 went green, 8 still red, 3 cancelled); **1 PR branches** needed both bot + human.\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>Sources: `gh api .../ci.yml/runs` (pass rates + rerun split via `.triggering_actor.login`), `az pipelines build list` def 1602 (internal, aggregate counts only), ciinsights MCP. Window = last 36h. Jul 7, 2026. **ciinsights ran degraded this run** — `get_health_summary` returned 0 builds for the 36h/7d window (its ingested data stops ~Jun 30), so failure **clusters** were confirmed from GH job logs directly, not ciinsights. Backlog & trend: see the weekly CI Health report (#18231). Generated 2026-07-07 06:12 UTC.</sub>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/aspire/issues/18232/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/aspire/issues/18232/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2/events","html_url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2","id":4148310390,"node_id":"I_kwDORx6c0M73QjF2","number":2,"title":"[BOUNTY $75] TEMPLATE: CLAUDE.md for a Next.js + SQLite SaaS project","user":{"login":"claudebounty","id":271393208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEC0huA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271393208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty","html_url":"https://github.com/claudebounty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10532402505,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e1SQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"D97706","default":false,"description":"Task with financial reward"},{"id":10532402633,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e1yQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/template","name":"template","color":"2563EB","default":false,"description":"Project template"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1076,"created_at":"2026-03-27T00:55:38Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:21:15Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 💰 Bounty: $75 — powered by [Opire](https://opire.dev)\n\n## Description\nCreate an opinionated, production-ready `CLAUDE.md` for a typical SaaS project\nbuilt with Next.js 15 App Router and SQLite (better-sqlite3 or Turso).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Covers: project structure, naming conventions, DB migration rules\n- [ ] Includes: dev commands, patterns to follow, anti-patterns to avoid\n- [ ] Opinionated — not generic. Every rule has a reason.\n- [ ] Usable without modification on a greenfield Next.js + SQLite project\n- [ ] Tested: create a new project, paste the CLAUDE.md, confirm Claude Code\n      understands the context without asking clarifying questions\n\n## How to Claim\n1. Comment `/opire try` in this issue\n2. Submit a PR with your CLAUDE.md\n3. Payment is released automatically on merge ✅\n\n## Expected Sections\n- Stack & versions\n- Folder structure\n- SQL / migration conventions\n- Component patterns\n- What we don't do (and why)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1","id":4148310244,"node_id":"I_kwDORx6c0M73QjDk","number":1,"title":"[BOUNTY $50] SKILL: Generate a structured CHANGELOG from git history","user":{"login":"claudebounty","id":271393208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEC0huA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271393208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty","html_url":"https://github.com/claudebounty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10532402505,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e1SQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"D97706","default":false,"description":"Task with financial reward"},{"id":10532402578,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e1kg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/skill","name":"skill","color":"7C3AED","default":false,"description":"Claude Code skill"},{"id":10532402781,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e2XQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"6EE7B7","default":true,"description":"Great for first-time contributors"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1704,"created_at":"2026-03-27T00:55:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:21:14Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 💰 Bounty: $50 — powered by [Opire](https://opire.dev)\n\n## Description\nCreate a Claude Code skill (`SKILL.md`) or a bash script that automatically generates\na structured `CHANGELOG.md` from a project's git history.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Works via `/generate-changelog` command or `bash changelog.sh`\n- [ ] Fetches commits since the last git tag\n- [ ] Auto-categorizes into: `Added` / `Fixed` / `Changed` / `Removed`\n- [ ] Outputs a properly formatted `CHANGELOG.md`\n- [ ] Tested on a real GitHub repo (include a sample output in the PR)\n- [ ] README with setup instructions in 3 steps or fewer\n\n## How to Claim\n1. Comment `/opire try` in this issue\n2. Submit a PR with your solution\n3. Payment is released automatically on merge ✅\n\n## Accepted Stack\nBash, Python, or native Claude Code `SKILL.md`.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/events","html_url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4","id":4148310747,"node_id":"I_kwDORx6c0M73QjLb","number":4,"title":"[BOUNTY $150] AGENT: Claude Code sub-agent that reviews a PR and posts a structured comment","user":{"login":"claudebounty","id":271393208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEC0huA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271393208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty","html_url":"https://github.com/claudebounty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10532402505,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e1SQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"D97706","default":false,"description":"Task with financial reward"},{"id":10532402697,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e2CQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/agent","name":"agent","color":"059669","default":false,"description":"Claude Code agent"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1065,"created_at":"2026-03-27T00:55:42Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:18:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 💰 Bounty: $150 — powered by [Opire](https://opire.dev)\n\n## Description\nCreate a Claude Code agent that takes a PR diff as input, analyzes it,\nand returns a structured Markdown review comment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Works via CLI: `claude-review --pr https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/123`\n- [ ] OR via GitHub Action (include the workflow YAML)\n- [ ] Structured Markdown output with:\n  - Summary of changes (2–3 sentences)\n  - Identified risks (list)\n  - Improvement suggestions (list)\n  - Confidence score: Low / Medium / High\n- [ ] Tested on at least 2 real GitHub PRs (include outputs in the PR)\n- [ ] README with setup and usage instructions\n\n## How to Claim\n1. Comment `/opire try` in this issue\n2. Submit a PR with the agent + sample outputs\n3. Payment is released automatically on merge ✅","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patchrail/patchrail/issues/69","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patchrail/patchrail","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patchrail/patchrail/issues/69/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patchrail/patchrail/issues/69/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patchrail/patchrail/issues/69/events","html_url":"https://github.com/patchrail/patchrail/issues/69","id":4579761472,"node_id":"I_kwDOSvXFAM8AAAABEPmdQA","number":69,"title":"Track real adoption and ecosystem signals for OSS program evidence","user":{"login":"PabloCodes7","id":284438953,"node_id":"U_kgDOEPQxqQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/284438953?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloCodes7","html_url":"https://github.com/PabloCodes7","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloCodes7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloCodes7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloCodes7/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloCodes7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloCodes7/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloCodes7/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloCodes7/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloCodes7/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloCodes7/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11125609033,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSvXFAM8AAAAClyNSSQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patchrail/patchrail/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true,"description":"Improvements or additions to documentation"},{"id":11127436344,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSvXFAM8AAAAClz80OA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patchrail/patchrail/labels/maintenance-workflow","name":"maintenance-workflow","color":"0052cc","default":false,"description":"Maintainer automation workflow or release process work"},{"id":11129282480,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSvXFAM8AAAACl1tfsA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patchrail/patchrail/labels/adopter-report","name":"adopter-report","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Consented external adopter or pilot feedback"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":38,"created_at":"2026-06-03T12:21:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:44:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Goal\n\nKeep PatchRail's public OSS evidence honest and current as real signals arrive.\n\n## Sources to update\n\n- docs/metrics.md\n- ADOPTERS.md\n- docs/openai-codex-for-oss-evidence.md\n- docs/oss-program-evidence.md\n- release evidence pages when a release changes the signal\n\n## Rules\n\n- Do not use placeholders as evidence.\n- Do not list external adopters without explicit permission.\n- Do not count private or unapproved pilots as public adoption.\n- Do not submit external program applications from placeholder metrics.\n\n## Done when\n\n- The first real PyPI install/download signal is recorded after #67.\n- The first consent-only pilot signal is recorded after #68.\n- Evidence pages distinguish verified metrics from pending goals.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patchrail/patchrail/issues/69/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/patchrail/patchrail/issues/69/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/events","html_url":"https://github.com/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770","id":4735571260,"node_id":"I_kwDORu6bf88AAAABGkMVPA","number":770,"title":"[BOUNTY $100] 🐜The Memanto Bug & Exploit Challenge","user":{"login":"Xenogents","id":68768092,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4NzY4MDky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68768092?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents","html_url":"https://github.com/Xenogents","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10849173787,"node_id":"LA_kwDORu6bf88AAAAChqlBGw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"fcf22a","default":false,"description":"This issue has a bounty attached to it"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":172,"created_at":"2026-06-24T14:09:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:13:35Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Description\nIn our last bounty, we asked the community to benchmark **Memanto** against the competition. You helped us prove that our active companion memory agent backed by our `moorcheh.ai` retrieval engine is uniquely resilient at handling shifting user preferences and maintaining long-term context without token bloat or memory degradation.\n\nNow, we are doing the exact opposite. \n\nWe believe Memanto is production-ready. But the best way to prove that is to invite the smartest engineers and red teamers to try and tear it down. \n\nWe are launching the **Memanto Bug Challenge** to uncover edge cases, logic loops, memory inconsistencies, and security vulnerabilities. If you can break our memory management, we want to know about it.\n\nThe Bounty: $100 USD (Paid via BountyHub)\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Threat Model & Scope\nYour target is the `memanto` core package and its interaction with the `moorcheh.ai` serverless backend. We are specifically looking for vulnerabilities and logic flaws that affect memory integrity, context window stability, and retrieval accuracy.\n\n### ✅ In Scope (What we want you to find)\n*   **Retrieval Quality & Accuracy:** Fails to recall highly relevant facts, loses track of when an event occurred (timeline amnesia), hallucinates sources, or fails to properly resolve direct contradictions.\n*   **Architectural & Logic Flaws:** Bad logic loops, poor contradiction handling, or inefficient background processes that severely slow down the agent.\n*   **Usability & Friction:** Is it too hard to set up? Are there major UX roadblocks preventing adoption?\n*   **Missing Core Features:** Missing support for critical use cases (e.g., lack of multi-agent support or complex workflows).\n*   **Security Vulnerabilities:** Any traditional security flaws, data leaks, or prompt injections.\n*   **Anything Else:** If you find a creative way to break or improve the memory layer, it's in scope!\n\n### 🚫 Out of Scope (Do not test these)\n*   Volumetric DDoS attacks against `moorcheh.ai` infrastructure.\n*   General LLM hallucinations unrelated to Memanto's memory handling.\n*   Attacks that require compromising the underlying operating system or Docker host to succeed.\n\n---\n\n### **🛠️ Implementation Guidelines:**\n\nTo ensure your submission qualifies for the bounty, your execution must follow this exact flow:\n\n*   **1. Find & Isolate:** Discover a bug, logic flaw, missing feature, or vulnerability within the Memanto core package.\n*   **2. Prove Reproducibility:** You must provide clear steps, a minimal Python script, or a test case that allows the maintainers to reproduce the bug exactly as you experienced it. If we can't reproduce it, we can't score it.\n*   **3. Implement the Fix (or Document the Flaw via PR):** Because this bounty is hosted on BountyHub, **all submissions must be Pull Requests.** We highly encourage writing the actual code to resolve the bug. However, if an issue requires massive architectural changes or involves backend systems you cannot fix from your end, you can still submit a PR! Instead of a code fix, submit a PR that adds a reproducible failing test script (e.g., to `tests/failing_tests/`) or a detailed Markdown report (e.g., to `docs/bounty_reports/`) outlining the problem and a proposed structural solution.\n\n### 📊 Judgment Method (The Success Matrix):\nTo ensure we reward actual engineering value and meaningful security research, submissions will be scored on a 100-point matrix split between **Technical Rigor** and **Impact**.\n\n| Criteria | Max Points | How it is Measured |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Severity & Impact** | 60 pts | How critical is the vulnerability, and does it affect a realistic production scenario? (e.g., highly relevant data corruption scores higher than a contrived edge case). |\n| **Reproducibility & Cleanliness** | 25 pts | Is the exploit perfectly replicable? Are scripts, dependency files, and clear instructions provided? Does the PoC work consistently? |\n| **Social Amplification** | 15 pts | Measured via public engagement metrics. |\n\n**The Social Formula:**\n\n`Social Points = (Reddit Upvotes x 4) + (Reddit Comments x 3) + (X Bookmarks x 5) + (X Retweets x 3) + (GitHub PR Reactions x 2)`\n\n### 🚨 Severity Guidelines\nWhile any bug or flaw is in scope, we prioritize and score based on the following guidelines for issue severity:\n\n| Severity | Description |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Critical / High** | Poor recall accuracy, losing track of timelines/dates, missing source attribution, deeply flawed contradiction handling, severe logic loops, major security vulnerabilities, or extreme performance bottlenecks (e.g., core systems freezing). |\n| **Medium** | Missing features (e.g., lacks multi-agent support), setup friction, UX roadblocks, or moderate inefficiencies that degrade the user experience. |\n| **Low** | Minor CLI/UI display bugs, non-critical feature requests, or simple documentation errors. |\n\n---\n\n### **🚀 Step-by-Step Instructions to Participate:**\n\n1. **Star the Repository:** Help us clear our next star milestone this month! ⭐️\n2. **Get Your Key:** Sign up at [moorcheh.ai](https://moorcheh.ai/) and configure your environment variables.\n3. **Hunt & Develop:** Identify a bug, feature gap, or logic flaw. Write a minimal script, test case, or detailed report demonstrating it.\n4. **Implement the Fix (or Document the Flaw):** Write the code to fix the vulnerability or add the missing feature. If the fix is too massive or simply cannot be fixed from your end (e.g., backend API issues), write a reproducible failing test script or a comprehensive Markdown report detailing the problem and your proposed solution.\n5. **Submit PR:** Fork this repo and create a Pull Request (required by BountyHub). Commit either your code fix, your failing test script, or your Markdown report. **Your PR description must contain a summary of the flaw, reproduction steps, and your fix or architectural proposal.** *(Note: If you uncover actual security vulnerabilities like data leaks, **do not open a public PR.** Please use GitHub's Private Vulnerability Reporting feature or email `support@moorcheh.ai` first).*\n6. **Amplify:** Write an in-depth post on Reddit or X and mention @moorcheh_ai showing off your deep dive into Memanto's architecture and how you improved it.\n\n> 📅 **Deadline:** All submissions must be submitted and active by **Aug 1, 2026 (11:59 PM UTC)** to be eligible for the success matrix audit.\n\n**Community and Support:** [Discord](https://discord.gg/CyxRFQSQ3p)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erniesg/paillette/issues/21","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erniesg/paillette","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erniesg/paillette/issues/21/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erniesg/paillette/issues/21/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erniesg/paillette/issues/21/events","html_url":"https://github.com/erniesg/paillette/issues/21","id":4724261931,"node_id":"I_kwDOQQepNM8AAAABGZaEKw","number":21,"title":"Launch Evidence And Rollback","user":{"login":"erniesg","id":7647813,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDc4MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7647813?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erniesg","html_url":"https://github.com/erniesg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erniesg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erniesg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erniesg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erniesg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erniesg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erniesg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erniesg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erniesg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erniesg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11312493156,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQQepNM8AAAACokbyZA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erniesg/paillette/labels/rucksack-ledger","name":"rucksack-ledger","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Rucksack-managed issue spec synced from docs/issues"},{"id":11312493987,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQQepNM8AAAACokb1ow","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erniesg/paillette/labels/rucksack-blocked","name":"rucksack-blocked","color":"B60205","default":false,"description":"Blocked or held by a human/operator decision"},{"id":11374970590,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQQepNM8AAAACpgBG3g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erniesg/paillette/labels/rucksack-waiting-rereview","name":"rucksack-waiting-rereview","color":"5319E7","default":false,"description":"Self-heal is waiting for reviewer re-review"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":19,"created_at":"2026-06-23T09:02:13Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T05:58:34Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- rucksack-issue-spec:006 -->\n<!-- rucksack-autopilot-depends-on:003,004,005,008 -->\n\n# Launch Evidence And Rollback\n\ndepends-on: 003,004,005,008\n\n## Goal\n\nCollect the evidence pack needed to launch the NGA collection and document rollback or disablement steps for data, assets, and search exposure.\n\n## Acceptance tests\n\n- Evidence links cover dry-run, D1 plan, asset plan, public search smoke, cost gate, and hosted unlock portal activation or hold decision.\n- `tmp/rucksack-human-gates-readiness.json` summarizes #26/#18/#20 readiness before launch review or repeated human pings.\n- Rollback notes identify how to hide the collection, remove queued batches, and delete staged object keys if needed.\n- No screenshots, manifests, or logs contain secret values.\n\n## Validation command\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/rucksack-human-gates-readiness.mjs --repo erniesg/paillette --manifest tmp/nga-launch-dry-run.json --out tmp/rucksack-human-gates-readiness.json\npnpm test\npnpm typecheck\n```\n\n## Allowed secrets\n\nNo secret values. Use only secret names and links to approved GitHub artifacts or object-store evidence.\n\n## Artifact outputs\n\n- `docs/nga-launch-readiness.md` launch checklist and evidence markdown.\n- `tmp/rucksack-human-gates-readiness.json` with current #26/#18/#20 missing names and decisions.\n- Search/API screenshot or JSON sample.\n- Rollback notes with reviewed commands in dry-run form.\n\n## Stop conditions\n\nStop before live launch if any upstream evidence issue is missing, if rollback is unclear, or if generated artifacts exceed storage policy.\n\n## Human clarification protocol\n\nAsk the human to approve live launch only after all evidence links and rollback notes are present. If #18 or #20 is not resolved, keep launch held and point to `docs/nga-launch-readiness.md` for the recommended v1 decision packet.\n\n## Recommended response\n\nSummarize launch readiness in one comment with links to evidence and a clear approve/hold decision path.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\nThe launch pack adds process overhead, but it gives autonomous agents a concrete definition of done for production-facing public art.\n\n## Free-form response\n\nAdd final launch caveats, unresolved risks, and the recommended approve/hold decision. The default hold decision is: defer vectors/caption generation, complete a bounded R2 staging upload first, then request launch approval with branch, environment, bucket, first batch size, and rollback owner.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erniesg/paillette/issues/21/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erniesg/paillette/issues/21/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auscaster/frantic-board/issues/106","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auscaster/frantic