aLabs/bug-bounty/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"cafa53","default":false,"description":""},{"id":10970820972,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSfPzA88AAAACjelxbA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/labels/%F0%9F%92%8E%20Bounty","name":"💎 Bounty","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11064514169,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSfPzA88AAAACk38WeQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/labels/$700","name":"$700","color":"34d399","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1377,"created_at":"2026-05-27T06:32:39Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T04:15:08Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Automate Low Hanging fruit bug detection and issue creation recursively.\n\nThis issue is an issue focused on creating more issues:\n1. Find a feature/bug to work on from this repository\n2. Create a GitHub issue on the repository to start working on it -- Pull requests without issues will not be considered.\n3. Use the following string in the issue that you created: \"This issue is limited only to the creator of this issue. This means that only the issue author can attempt to solve this issue. If you would like to work on it, please create another issue with the same contents and refer to issue #743 for more information.\"\n\nFollow all instructions carefully and precisely.\n\n/bounty $700\n\nBounties can only be paid upon successful PR merge.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SauersML/gam/issues/979","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SauersML/gam","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SauersML/gam/issues/979/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SauersML/gam/issues/979/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SauersML/gam/issues/979/events","html_url":"https://github.com/SauersML/gam/issues/979","id":4625780456,"node_id":"I_kwDORXZ1mc8AAAABE7fO6A","number":979,"title":"marginal-slope (binary + survival) bug: severe slowdown / survival hang in gamfit 0.1.189","user":{"login":"SauersML","id":123714540,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-77A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123714540?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SauersML","html_url":"https://github.com/SauersML","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SauersML/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SauersML/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SauersML/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SauersML/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SauersML/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SauersML/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SauersML/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SauersML/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SauersML/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":241,"created_at":"2026-06-09T21:32:52Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T04:05:34Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\nOn **gamfit 0.1.189** (PyPI), `marginal-slope` fits regressed badly versus an earlier version (~0.1.156) that completed the *same* fits in the *same* pipeline:\n\n1. **`bernoulli-marginal-slope` is now extremely slow** — fits that used to take seconds now spend tens of seconds just in the outer \"continuation pre-warm\", and at `centers=20` do not finish within a 20–33 min window.\n2. **`survival_likelihood=\"marginal-slope\"` now HANGS** (runs to a hard timeout with no output) rather than completing or raising. A hang is worse than the old crash (gam#751) because a `try/except` can't catch it, so it also blocks the Cox baselines run in the same script.\n\n## Minimal repro (binary slowdown)\n\n```python\nimport signal, time, pandas as pd, gamfit\nd = pd.read_parquet(\"serial1d_phenoA_realpt_s1.parquet\")     # n~2500, K=2 PCs, real P+T score\nfit = d[d[\"split\"].astype(str).str.contains(\"fit\")]\ndata = {\"z\": fit[\"PGS_z\"].to_numpy(float), \"PC1\": fit[\"PC1\"].to_numpy(float),\n        \"PC2\": fit[\"PC2\"].to_numpy(float), \"event\": fit[\"y_binary\"].to_numpy(float)}\nt = time.time()\ngamfit.fit(data, formula=\"event ~ matern(PC1, PC2, centers=4)\",\n           family=\"bernoulli-marginal-slope\", link=\"probit\",\n           z_column=\"z\", logslope_formula=\"matern(PC1, PC2, centers=4)\")\nprint(\"secs\", round(time.time()-t,1))\n```\n\nEven at **centers=4** the fit progresses but is slow; the outer log shows:\n\n```\n[28s] [PIRLS/joint-Newton terminal] converged=true terminator=KKT/certificate-converged cycles=17/21 ...\n[36s] [OUTER] custom family: continuation pre-warm seed 0 steps=4 elapsed=34.415s\n```\n\ni.e. ~35 s elapsed just for \"continuation pre-warm seed 0\" at centers=4. At **centers=20** (a normal setting) the fit did not complete within 20–33 min in a 24-way parallel batch.\n\n## Survival hang\n\nSame data, `gamfit.fit(..., family/survival_likelihood=\"marginal-slope\", Surv(time,event), matern(PCs, centers=12))`: every cell ran to a 2000 s timeout (`rc=124`) producing no output — a hang, not a raise.\n\n## Impact\n\nA multi-seed real-PGS cross-ancestry calibration study that completed end-to-end on ~0.1.156 is impractical on 0.1.189: binary `centers=20` fits don't finish in reasonable time and survival fits hang.\n\n## Environment\n\ngamfit 0.1.189 (PyPI wheel), Python 3.11, Linux. `matern` over 2–3 PCs, `bernoulli-marginal-slope` (probit) and survival `marginal-slope`, no link/score/time wiggle, `centers ∈ {4, 12, 20}`. The heavy time is in the marginal-slope inner solve / continuation pre-warm (the machinery added across 0.1.18x for #808/#787/#729/#691).\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SauersML/gam/issues/979/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SauersML/gam/issues/979/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlutterFlow/flutterflow-issues/issues/7247","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlutterFlow/flutterflow-issues","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlutterFlow/flutterflow-issues/issues/7247/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlutterFlow/flutterflow-issues/issues/7247/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlutterFlow/flutterflow-issues/issues/7247/events","html_url":"https://github.com/FlutterFlow/flutterflow-issues/issues/7247","id":4740389158,"node_id":"I_kwDOH2qCQM8AAAABGoyZJg","number":7247,"title":"URGENT: FlutterFlow Desktop crashes when opening my project, blocking Local Run testing","user":{"login":"hekinha97ipartiu","id":294302976,"node_id":"U_kgDOEYq1AA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294302976?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hekinha97ipartiu","html_url":"https://github.com/hekinha97ipartiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hekinha97ipartiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hekinha97ipartiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hekinha97ipartiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hekinha97ipartiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hekinha97ipartiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hekinha97ipartiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hekinha97ipartiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hekinha97ipartiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hekinha97ipartiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":4446815928,"node_id":"LA_kwDOH2qCQM8AAAABCQ0GuA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlutterFlow/flutterflow-issues/labels/type:%20bug","name":"type: bug","color":"d73a4a","default":false,"description":"Something isn't working."},{"id":4464309358,"node_id":"LA_kwDOH2qCQM8AAAABChf0bg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlutterFlow/flutterflow-issues/labels/status:%20confirmed","name":"status: confirmed","color":"bec2c8","default":false,"description":"Issue has been reproduced and confirmed as a bug."},{"id":6974622474,"node_id":"LA_kwDOH2qCQM8AAAABn7hLCg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlutterFlow/flutterflow-issues/labels/Windows","name":"Windows","color":"26b5ce","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"sbis04","id":43280874,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMjgwODc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43280874?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04","html_url":"https://github.com/sbis04","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-06-25T03:37:58Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T04:02:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"sbis04","id":43280874,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMjgwODc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43280874?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04","html_url":"https://github.com/sbis04","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbis04/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Can we access your project?\n\n- [x] I give permission for members of the FlutterFlow team to access and test my project for the sole purpose of investigating this issue.\n\n### Current Behavior\n\nHi FlutterFlow team,\n\nThis is urgent because FlutterFlow Desktop is crashing when opening my project, and this is blocking me from using Local Run to test on a physical phone.\n\nProject ID: i-partiu-iw075t\nProject name: iPartiu\n\nFlutterFlow Desktop crashes only when opening this existing project. New/empty projects open normally.\n\nCrash details from Windows Event Viewer:\n\nApp: flutterflow.exe\nVersion: 7.0.11.0\nFaulting module: flutter_inappwebview_windows_plugin.dll\nException code: 0xc0000005\nFault offset: 0x000000000007aff5\nPath: C:\\Program Files\\FlutterFlow\\flutterflow.exe\n\nThe project opens in the browser, but the desktop app crashes while loading it. I urgently need Desktop because I rely on Local Run to test on a physical phone.\n\nI already tried:\n- duplicating the project\n- excluding the custom widget MapaRota from compilation\n- removing GoogleMap from the page in the duplicated project\n- reinstalling FlutterFlow Desktop\n- trying older desktop versions, but the project requires the newer version\n\nThe crash still happens with the duplicated project.\n\nPlease urgently help identify what in the project is triggering this WebView crash, or repair/restore the project so it can open in FlutterFlow Desktop again.\n\nI can provide screenshots and Windows Event Viewer logs if needed.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\ni need to open flutterflow app to run test in local host for use my phone\n(tests on Google Chrome e Firefox has crash in CORS when i'm trying to pick my localization on GOOGLE MAPS API).\nbut the app on my desktop closes when trying to compilation my project.\ni try to desinstall and install again, usyng codex for help but withou solution at all.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. open flutterflow desktop app\n2. try to open my project iPartiu\n3. wait for compilation .... then he closes alone\n\n### Reproducible from Blank\n\n- [ ] The steps to reproduce above start from a blank project.\n\n### Bug Report Code (Required)\n\nThe crash is not tied to a specific widget. The desktop app crashes while loading the project. I generated the report code from a random Scaffold/widget because the form requires it.\n\n### Visual documentation\n\n<!-- Failed to upload \"prove.mp4\" -->\n\n### Environment\n\n```markdown\n- FlutterFlow version: \n- Platform:\n- Browser name and version:\n- Operating system and version affected:\n```\n\n### Additional Information\n\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlutterFlow/flutterflow-issues/issues/7247/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlutterFlow/flutterflow-issues/issues/7247/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/66391","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/66391/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/66391/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/66391/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues/66391","id":3237318546,"node_id":"I_kwDOEQqHYc7A9Y-S","number":66391,"title":"[Due for payment 2026-07-13] Remove `Onyx.connect()` for the key: `ONYXKEYS.PERSONAL_DETAILS_LIST` in `src/libs/PersonalDetailsUtils.ts`","user":{"login":"tgolen","id":1228807,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjg4MDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1228807?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen","html_url":"https://github.com/tgolen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgolen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":2283143991,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMjgzMTQzOTkx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/Reviewing","name":"Reviewing","color":"dddddd","default":false,"description":"Has a PR in review"},{"id":2873635554,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODczNjM1NTU0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/Engineering","name":"Engineering","color":"274073","default":false,"description":""},{"id":2893515375,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODkzNTE1Mzc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/Weekly","name":"Weekly","color":"009800","default":false,"description":"KSv2"},{"id":2893524800,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODkzNTI0ODAw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/Improvement","name":"Improvement","color":"604c8d","default":false,"description":"Item broken or needs improvement."},{"id":3271255930,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjcxMjU1OTMw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/Awaiting%20Payment","name":"Awaiting Payment","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":"Auto-added when associated PR is deployed to production"},{"id":3409213164,"node_id":"LA_kwDOEQqHYc7LNHbs","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/Not%20a%20priority","name":"Not a priority","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":4664850679,"node_id":"LA_kwDOEQqHYc8AAAABFgv49w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/Bug","name":"Bug","color":"93074F","default":false,"description":"Something is broken. Auto assigns a BugZero manager."}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"mountiny","id":36083550,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDgzNTUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36083550?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny","html_url":"https://github.com/mountiny","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"bernhardoj","id":50919443,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwOTE5NDQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50919443?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bernhardoj","html_url":"https://github.com/bernhardoj","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bernhardoj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bernhardoj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bernhardoj/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bernhardoj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bernhardoj/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bernhardoj/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bernhardoj/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bernhardoj/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bernhardoj/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"shubham1206agra","id":58412969,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NDEyOTY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58412969?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shubham1206agra","html_url":"https://github.com/shubham1206agra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shubham1206agra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shubham1206agra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shubham1206agra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shubham1206agra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shubham1206agra/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shubham1206agra/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shubham1206agra/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shubham1206agra/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shubham1206agra/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":43,"created_at":"2025-07-16T20:47:47Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T03:57:21Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"mountiny","id":36083550,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDgzNTUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36083550?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny","html_url":"https://github.com/mountiny","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mountiny/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/66390","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This is part of deprecating Onyx.connect. [Parent Issue](https://github.com/Expensify/Expensify/issues/522215)\n\n## Details\n- **Module**: [src/libs/PersonalDetailsUtils.ts](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/main/src/libs/PersonalDetailsUtils.ts)\n- **Onyx Key**: `ONYXKEYS.PERSONAL_DETAILS_LIST`\n- **Reference**: `Line 24: ONYXKEYS.PERSONAL_DETAILS_LIST`\n\nBe sure to refactor methods using test driven development:\n1. Create a unit test for methods before refactoring\n2. Refactor the methods\n3. Ensure the unit test still runs after refactoring\n4. Reinforce the unit testing with a functional test and a QA test\n5. Once you are done, decrease the number of allowable ESLint warnings [here](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/e7b5ac9401e2ae9b5c2c70ec513e8de6f5279d7d/package.json#L48) to equal the number of `Onyx.connect` references remaining in the code\n\n<details><summary>Issue Owner</summary>Current Issue Owner: @bernhardoj</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/66391/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/66391/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer/issues/115","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer/issues/115/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer/issues/115/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer/issues/115/events","html_url":"https://github.com/TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer/issues/115","id":4544455024,"node_id":"I_kwDOP4AlL88AAAABDt7hcA","number":115,"title":"SESSION-PRIME: paste body's fenced block into a fresh Claude session to orient fast","user":{"login":"TortoiseWolfe","id":101219421,"node_id":"U_kgDOBgh8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101219421?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TortoiseWolfe","html_url":"https://github.com/TortoiseWolfe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TortoiseWolfe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TortoiseWolfe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TortoiseWolfe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TortoiseWolfe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TortoiseWolfe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TortoiseWolfe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TortoiseWolfe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TortoiseWolfe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TortoiseWolfe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9361552873,"node_id":"LA_kwDOP4AlL88AAAACLf316Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true,"description":"Improvements or additions to documentation"},{"id":11081533272,"node_id":"LA_kwDOP4AlL88AAAAClILHWA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer/labels/next-session","name":"next-session","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Rolling priming prompt for new sessions"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":43,"created_at":"2026-05-28T23:14:01Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T03:49:24Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Purpose:** this issue is the durable roadmap for TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer (the template). The body below is always-current — active arc, next 3 sessions queued, backlog. Comments are the audit trail. The prime prompt at the top tells a fresh Claude session to read this body first.\n\n> ✅ **Updated 2026-07-05.** The **basePath E2E hardening arc (#157/#158/#159) is COMPLETE** — shipped as PRs TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer#176/#177/#178. With it, the entire multi-session PAYMENTS → CI → DB → basePath backlog is **fully drained**. There is no queued engineering thread left; the next session is a clean **product-direction pivot** (user's call). See the latest comment for the audit trail.\n\n---\n\n## Prime prompt (copy from here into a fresh Claude session)\n\n```\n/prep\n\nThen check this issue (TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer#115) — its BODY is the current roadmap. Read everything below the prime prompt: active arc, next 3 sessions queued, backlog. The most recent COMMENT on this issue is the audit trail of what changed since the previous session.\n\nSupplementary context (read if the body's roadmap references them or if the user's first message takes us off-roadmap):\n1. `~/.claude/projects/-home-TurtleWolfe-repos-ScriptHammer/memory/MEMORY.md` — top of the index lists NON-NEGOTIABLE user preferences + recently-banked lessons. Read these first; they're binding.\n2. `git log --oneline -20` — what shipped recently.\n3. Open issues (`gh issue list --repo TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer --state open`) — most are tagged `template-v1-out-of-scope` (Eval-Backlog / Gap-Audit); treat those as deferred backlog. (RescueDogs-fork bugs once misfiled here were transferred to the fork — its roadmap is TortoiseWolfe/RescueDogs#5.)\n4. Open PRs (`gh pr list --repo TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer --state open`).\n\nOperational reminders from MEMORY.md / CLAUDE.md you'll trip over otherwise:\n- ALWAYS prefer cleaner long-term solutions over quick hacks. Never offer a hack as the primary recommendation. Fix root cause, not symptoms.\n- TWO local checkouts push to related repos: ~/repos/ScriptHammer → TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer (THIS roadmap), ~/repos/RescueDogs → TortoiseWolfe/RescueDogs (roadmap = RescueDogs#5). A fork session once overwrote this body by accident — confirm which checkout you're in before running /session-prime.\n- CI honesty: a green job `conclusion` ≠ 0 flaky — `retries:2` masks retry-recovered failures. ALWAYS read per-job `flaky`/`failed` lines + `gh api .../commits/<sha>/check-runs` annotations before claiming clean or merging. (The lone `Test Report` annotation is a `notice` with the pass/skip count — that's clean.)\n- Local live-acceptance E2E runbook (root-path build, serve on :3001 — the fn CORS allowlist —, SKIP_WEBSERVER+BASE_URL, seeded env-driven users): see [[lesson_e2e_live_acceptance_mechanics]]. basePath-served E2E (the PREFIXED sibling): [[lesson_basepath_e2e_project]] + `scripts/serve-basepath.sh` (`--project=basepath`).\n- Edge fns read NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_* names the platform does NOT auto-inject — set as fn secrets via `pnpm supabase:secrets`. NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL fn secret IS set (scripthammer.com). See [[lesson_stripe_clover_and_fn_env]].\n- Pushing to `.github/workflows/**` needs SSH (gh HTTPS token lacks `workflow` scope). If the session's ssh-agent is empty, probe `/tmp/ssh-*/agent.*` sockets and export the one that authenticates.\n- Supabase prod can DRIFT from the monolithic migration. Verify schema/triggers against the LIVE DB, never trust issue text or the migration file alone. Mgmt API DDL: build the JSON payload from a FILE. Edge-fn deploys are CLI-free via the Management API (see [[lesson_edge_function_deploy_management_api]]); regenerate types via GET /v1/projects/{ref}/types/typescript.\n- CI mutex serializes E2E runs; PR E2E is chromium-only (firefox/webkit on push-to-main + cron, or the `full-e2e` PR label). A merge to main kicks off a full push-to-main E2E that holds the mutex, so the NEXT PR's E2E queues behind it (~30-60 min) — expected, not a hang. docs/`.claude`/`.specify`/`features`/md changes skip E2E (paths-ignore). `--admin` merge is OK when all gates+smoke are green and only unrelated chromium-gen shards (or a documented unrelated retry-recovered flake) remain.\n- The container's `.env` has `NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/ScriptHammer`, so any local build/test regenerates `public/manifest.json` with the prefix — a build side-effect. REVERT it before every commit; it is never part of a PR.\n\nThen either start on the roadmap's \"next session should\" item, or ask the user if they want to deviate.\n```\n\n## Stop reading here when priming — everything below is the roadmap\n\n---\n\n## Roadmap\n\n### Active arc\n\n**VERIFICATION HANDOFF + PICK THE NEXT PRODUCT DIRECTION** — the payment/E2E backlog (#188 → #189-197) shipped and closed this session. Two open issues (#188, #212) are now in a **human-verification** phase handed to collaborator `schlajo`; once those close, the tracked eng backlog is fully drained and the next arc is a user product call.\n\nStatus: **payment backlog drained; 2 issues awaiting schlajo's verification; 1 docs PR open.** Open issues: #188 (confirm backlog drained — REOPENED after a premature close, awaiting independent verification), #212 (label/input gap — needs rendered screenshots; code audit says fork-only), #205 (flaky-watch marker), #115 (this roadmap). Open PR: **#213** (schlajo verification runbook, docs-only). The 9 payment/CI tickets (#189-197) all merged with `main` green across chromium+firefox+webkit (final commit `ccdc86c`).\n\nRemaining tasks (in suggested order):\n- [ ] **Assign #188 + #212 to schlajo once he accepts the repo invite** (Read; pending — GitHub blocks assignment until acceptance). Commands in `docs/verification/schlajo-tickets.md` + [[pending_schlajo_assignment]].\n- [ ] Merge PR #213 (docs verification runbook) — docs-only, no E2E gate.\n- [ ] On schlajo's verdict: close #188 if confirmed drained; for #212, transfer to RescueDogs if fork-only, or fix here if screenshots show a real ScriptHammer cram.\n- [ ] Then ask the user for the next product goal, OR enable a provider-supplied key (Sentry #45 / Resend).\n\nBlockers / decisions needed:\n- **#188/#212 assignment is blocked on schlajo accepting the invite** (invite id `324802601`, Read). Everything else (Cursor prompts, runbook) is already in place.\n- **Next product arc is the user's call** once verification closes out.\n\n---\n\n### Next 3 sessions queued\n\nNothing is force-ordered. In rough priority, the next sessions should pick from:\n\n**Session +1:** Close out the verification handoff (#188, #212, PR #213)\n- Why: two issues are mid-verification with schlajo; PR #213 is open. Resolving these returns the tracker to a true zero-backlog state.\n- First action: check if schlajo accepted the invite (`gh api repos/TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer/collaborators/schlajo`); if yes, assign #188+#212; merge PR #213; act on any verification findings he posted.\n\n**Session +2:** New product arc (user-directed)\n- Why: with verification closed, this is the clean point to pick a new feature direction. A driving app (e.g. HatCoatAndBoots) or a new template capability both qualify.\n- First action: ask the user what the next product goal is, then run the SpecKit/PRP flow for anything >1 day.\n\n**Session +3:** Provider-supplied enablement (Sentry DSN TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer#45, RESEND_API_KEY)\n- Why: two features are code-complete and inert pending a user-supplied key — zero engineering, just set the secret + verify activation.\n- First action: once the user provides a Sentry DSN and/or Resend key, set it (Actions secret / Vault) and confirm the feature activates live.\n\n---\n\n### Backlog (no scheduled position)\n\n- **#182 — group message E2E encryption — SHIPPED** (PR TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer#185, `b1ee9ad`, 2026-07-05). Wired the group key into all 5 message-service stubs (send/edit/decrypt keyed by per-message `key_version`; archive/unarchive via `conversation_members.archived`) + fixed 3 pre-existing group-creation RLS gaps that made groups unreachable (conversations INSERT+SELECT, conversation_members SELECT creator-clause) — all applied live + verified. Group E2E is skip-tolerant (heavy Argon2/ECDH); logic covered by unit tests. See [[lesson_group_messaging_rls_and_e2e]].\n- **Follow-up (small): deterministic group send/decrypt E2E** — the current group E2E skips on slow runners (UI-creation does in-browser key distribution >90s). A seed-group-server-side variant (replicating ECDH key distribution in the fixture) would give a non-skipping send/decrypt test. Nice-to-have.\n- **#183 — remove the unused `oauth_states` CSRF layer — SHIPPED** (PR TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer#184, `4ad49ca`, 2026-07-05). Deleted the dead module+test, edited the monolith, live-dropped the prod table (0 rows, 4 public policies), regen types. Also corrected the OAuth blog + `OAuthButtons` comment: the app uses `flowType: 'implicit'` (static export), CSRF = Supabase's OAuth2 `state` — NOT PKCE (old comments were wrong).\n- **blog-data.json drift** — several posts' committed titles/ids are stale vs source `.md` (surfaced during TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer#184, which only re-synced the OAuth post). Standalone `pnpm run generate:blog` resync + commit; small, mechanical.\n- **Sentry DSN → flip TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer#45 live** — user creates a sentry.io project, sets `NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN` in `.env` + Actions secret. Monitoring activates post-consent with zero code change.\n- **RESEND_API_KEY → send-payment-email** — set as a fn secret; the payment-email edge fn is deployed but inert without it.\n- **Payment/E2E backlog #188 (#189-197) — SHIPPED 2026-07-06/07.** Skip-hygiene sweep (#187) turned \"82 skipped\" into a code-verified backlog, then shipped it all: GDPR consent-reset (#189/#200), offline-queue quota warning (#190/#201), realtime reconnect/batch/error (#191-193/#203/#206/#208), payment trend chart (#194/#209), subscription dunning + deployed `retry-subscription` edge fn (#195/#210), Keep-Alive pnpm-order CI fix (#196/#211), and the keystone unpaginated-`listUsers` fix (#197/#202 — \"test user not found\" was pagination, NOT a race). All merged; `main` green on all 3 browsers @ `ccdc86c`. What remains skipped is 53 runtime guards + 12 permanent creds/feature markers (Stripe/PayPal live-Checkout) — NOT debt.\n- **schlajo verification handoff (OPEN)** — #188 (confirm drained) + #212 (label/input gap, needs screenshots) assigned-pending to collaborator `schlajo` (Read invite, not yet accepted). Cursor prompts on both issues + `docs/verification/schlajo-tickets.md` (PR #213). Assign once he accepts: [[pending_schlajo_assignment]].\n- **#212 label/input gap** — filed from the RescueDogs fork; a 4-reader audit found ScriptHammer's auth forms already stack labels above inputs (no cram). Needs rendered screenshots at 320/768/1280px to confirm; if fork-only → transfer to RescueDogs, else fix. (Was #199 → transferred to RescueDogs#20 → transferred back as #212.)\n- **Gap-audit items TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer#38/#35/#25 — CLOSED** (gap-audit workflow, 2026-07-05): all resolved as already-done or fork-scope (not template debt). Not backlog anymore; kept here only as a pointer that the tier-2 gap-audit is drained.\n- **Follow-up (small): deterministic group send/decrypt E2E** — see the group-messaging note above; seed-group-server-side variant so it doesn't skip on slow runners. Nice-to-have.\n- **E2E flaky watch (#205)** — `oauth-csrf.spec.ts:78` webkit (live github.com nav), `messaging-scroll.spec.ts:292`, blog-TOC / color-contrast / message-editing a11y. All retry-recover; harden if noisy. Tracked as a marker, not work.\n- **Reusable substrate (on main):** `scripts/serve-basepath.sh` + the `basepath` Playwright project (basePath-served E2E, TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer#157); `getInternalUrl`/`getRedirectUrl` basePath helpers; the `DISABLE_BASE_PATH` E2E harness switch (#158); `pnpm supabase:secrets` (Vault, CLI-free); the live-acceptance runbook; `embed-theme.ts` + `useEmbedThemeColor`; `EmailProviderHealth`; the unified `/payment` hub (`?tab=` deep-link); `idx_subscriptions_one_live_per_user` dup-guard; `PaymentQueuePanel`; `useConnections` realtime-badge pattern; `startFormQueueFallback`. **New this session:** `usePaymentResultsRealtime` (additive `onBatch?`/`onEvent?` callbacks); `aggregate-daily.ts` + `PaymentTrendChart`; the `retry-subscription` edge fn (deployed, dunning-schedule advance); paginated `listUsers` throughout `global-setup.ts`/`test-user-factory.ts` (the >50-users gate fix); `seedIsolatedSubscription`/`openSubscriptionsAs` fixtures; cross-browser E2E patterns (offline-event dispatch for FF/WebKit, `defineProperty` for WebKit `navigator.storage`).\n\n---\n\n### Next session should\n\n**Close out the schlajo verification handoff, then ask the user for a new product direction.** First: check whether schlajo accepted the repo invite (`gh api repos/TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer/collaborators/schlajo`) — if yes, assign #188 + #212 to him (`gh issue edit … --add-assignee schlajo`); merge PR #213 (docs runbook); act on any verification findings. Once #188/#212 resolve, the tracked eng backlog is fully drained (payment/CI/DB/basePath + #181 review + both follow-ups all shipped), and the next arc is a user product call — a new feature, a driving-app pull (HatCoatAndBoots), or flipping Sentry #45 / Resend live with a user-supplied key. Confirm the goal before inventing an arc.\n\n---\n\n## Why this exists\n\nSessions end. The next session starts cold. Without a single canonical \"what was the world like when we last stopped + here's what to do next\" pointer, the new model wastes context wandering. This issue is the one URL to paste into a fresh chat. The BODY carries the plan; comments form the audit trail.\n\n## How to maintain\n\nRun `/session-prime` at session-end. The skill rewrites the body to reflect what changed in the roadmap and appends a comment with the audit trail. **This issue is the TEMPLATE's roadmap — RescueDogs-fork sessions must use TortoiseWolfe/RescueDogs#5 instead.**\n\nIf the prime prompt itself becomes stale (memory file renamed, project changed shape), edit the body's prime-prompt block directly.\n\n\n\n\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer/issues/115/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TortoiseWolfe/ScriptHammer/issues/115/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/83257","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/83257/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/83257/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/83257/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues/83257","id":3980494114,"node_id":"I_kwDOEQqHYc7tQYUi","number":83257,"title":"[$250] Expense - Different destination opens when bulk merging vs merging individually","user":{"login":"mitarachim","id":181838622,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtajHg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181838622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitarachim","html_url":"https://github.com/mitarachim","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitarachim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitarachim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitarachim/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitarachim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/us